	<h2>What are we trying to do here?</h2>
	<p>
		Consumer goods companies sell many brands, across several countries and many kinds of shops: large
		retailers, convenience stores, online and small traditional stores. Their leaders get dozens of
		reports, each cut a different way. Most of their review time goes into reconciling numbers instead
		of deciding what to do.
	</p>
	<p>
		This experiment asks a simple question: <strong>what would one page look like that a CEO, CFO, CMO,
		Head of Sales or COO could open each week and immediately know where to act?</strong>
	</p>
	<p>The page is built around the sequence leaders actually think in:</p>
	<ol>
		<li><strong>Health</strong>: are we on track against plan, last year and the market?</li>
		<li><strong>Deviation</strong>: where are the biggest gaps, good and bad?</li>
		<li><strong>Drivers</strong>: what is causing them: price, volume, promotions, costs, supply or competitors?</li>
		<li><strong>Implications</strong>: is it us or the market, and what does it mean for the year?</li>
		<li><strong>Action</strong>: what should we do next, and who owns it?</li>
	</ol>

	<h2>How it works</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Every role shares the same headline numbers, so the CEO and CFO see the same thing in the same meeting.</li>
		<li>Each role then gets its own view, ordered around the decisions that role makes.</li>
		<li>The page leads with the few deviations that matter most, not every metric available.</li>
		<li>Clicking any number opens only the detail behind that question, down to a brand, market, retailer or promotion.</li>
		<li>Short summaries explain what changed and suggest a likely cause and next step. In this prototype they are generated by rules.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>About the data</h2>
	<p>
		The company, its brands, retailers, competitors and every number are fictional. The data is
		generated with a handful of business stories built in, such as a competitor price cut, growth bought
		through deep discounts and a supply disruption, to test whether each leader can find their story
		within a few clicks.
	</p>

